    <!-- Phase explainers, for the partner who doesn\'t have a cycle -->
    <string name="phase_about_menstrual">The period itself — the uterine lining sheds. Estrogen and progesterone are at their lowest, so energy and mood often dip.</string>
    <string name="phase_about_follicular">After the period, estrogen climbs as the body prepares to release an egg. Energy, mood, and motivation rise through this phase.</string>
    <string name="phase_about_ovulation">Estrogen peaks and an egg is released — the fertile window. Many feel their most confident, social, and energetic.</string>
    <string name="phase_about_luteal">After ovulation, progesterone rises then falls toward the next period. Energy winds down and PMS can appear in the last few days.</string>
    <string name="phase_symptoms_menstrual">Cramps, fatigue, low mood, headaches, and cravings are common. Rest matters most now.</string>
    <string name="phase_symptoms_follicular">Usually the easiest stretch — mostly higher energy. Some notice restlessness or skin changes.</string>
    <string name="phase_symptoms_ovulation">Peak energy and libido; some feel mild cramping or bloating around release.</string>
    <string name="phase_symptoms_luteal">Tiredness, mood swings, irritability, bloating, cravings, and tender breasts — strongest just before the period.</string>

    <!-- The rest of each phase\'s partner tips (the first of each is above) -->
    <string name="phase_tip_menstrual_2">Offer a heating pad and let her rest</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_menstrual_3">Quietly take chores off her plate</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_menstrual_4">Be patient — low energy and cramps are normal</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_follicular_2">Great week for a date or trying something new together</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_follicular_3">Match her upbeat, motivated mood</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_ovulation_2">Extra affection and compliments land really well now</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_ovulation_3">If you\'re trying for a baby, this is the fertile window</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_luteal_2">Cook or handle dinner</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_luteal_3">Give extra reassurance, patience, and cuddles</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_luteal_4">Bring her comfort food or chocolate</string>
    <string name="phase_tip_luteal_5">Don\'t take small mood shifts personally</string>

